lsrecent (1.7.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * The cd prompt is now a browser: search by name or path, page with +, show
    everything with a, ? for help. A bare word searches; digits still select.
  * Numbers remain ranking positions under filtering and paging, so a number
    means the same repository everywhere and in `lsrecent path N` later.
  * Reaches the entries below the fold, which previously required abandoning
    the listing for `lsrepos --all` or the fzf picker.

 -- Daniel Rosehill <daniel@danielrosehill.co.il>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 16:05:00 +0300

lsrecent (1.6.0) unstable; urgency=low

  * Add lsrecent-gui, a PyQt6 window for adding and removing directories from
    the include-list, and `lsrecent gui` / a desktop entry to reach it.
  * Add `lsrecent shell-install`, so the per-user ~/.bashrc edit lives in the
    binary rather than only in install.sh — the .deb has no install.sh.
  * remove: delete the entry with grep -vxF instead of an interpolated sed
    address, which failed on any path containing the sed delimiter and
    reported success anyway.
  * Ship as a .deb (build-deb.sh).

 -- Daniel Rosehill <daniel@danielrosehill.co.il>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:30:00 +0300

lsrecent (1.5.1) unstable; urgency=low

  * Say when the cd prompt is missing because the shell integration predates
    the binary: shell-init exports LSRECENT_SHELL and the binary compares it.
  * --version reports both halves of the pair.

 -- Daniel Rosehill <daniel@danielrosehill.co.il>  Thu, 30 Jul 2026 15:10:00 +0300

